OL,3,ACeremony marks return home of kiwi
OL,4,Afeather cloak
OL,5,
OL,6,FA ceremony has been held to mark the
OL,7,Freturn of a MDAori kiwi feather cloak
OL,8,Fto New Zealand by a British museum.
OL,10,FThe kahu kiwi was one of the farewell
OL,11,Fgifts presented by MDAori leaders in
OL,12,F1900 to Dr George Cleghorn, a medical
OL,13,Fdoctor who had been working in New
OL,14,FZealand.
OL,16,FIt was loaned to the Pitt Rivers Museum
OL,17,Fin Oxford by Cleghorn's widow in 1913.
OL,19,FThe return was organised by the charity
OL,20,Fthe Homebound Project which specialises
OL,21,Fin reuniting indigenous artefacts with
OL,22,Ftheir country of origin.
OL,23,APub: 10-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
